subproblem.statement:
Let g : ℝ^N → ℝ be continuous with compact support. Then there exist a compact set K ⊆ ℝ^N and functions φ_k : ℝ^N → ℝ (k ∈ ℕ) such that:
- g(y) = 0 for every y ∉ K;
- every φ_k is C¹;
- φ_k(y) = 0 for every k and every y ∉ K;
- for every ε > 0 there is k₀ ∈ ℕ with |φ_k(y) − g(y)| ≤ ε for all k ≥ k₀ and all y ∈ ℝ^N.
